      "Dark mode compatibility is no longer a nice-to-have. Over 80% of mobile email opens now happen with dark mode enabled, and a newsletter that looks great in light mode but becomes unreadable in dark mode is losing a significant portion of its audience. This means transparent PNGs instead of JPEGs with white backgrounds, explicit background colors on every element instead of relying on white defaults, and testing in both modes before every send. Use border colors that work on both light and dark backgrounds.",
      "AMP for email has finally reached critical mass. Gmail, Yahoo, and Mail.ru all support AMP components, which means your newsletter can include live polls, image carousels, accordion sections, and real-time content that updates after delivery. Readers no longer need to click through to your website to take action — they can RSVP to an event, answer a survey, or browse products directly within the email. Early adopters report 3x higher engagement rates compared to static emails.",
      "Accessibility has moved from aspiration to expectation. Screen readers now handle email more gracefully, but only if the email is properly structured. Every image needs meaningful alt text, not just the filename. Color contrast ratios must meet WCAG AA standards — particularly important for your gold-on-dark-background accent colors. Use semantic HTML: headings in order, proper list markup, and link text that describes the destination rather than 'click here'. Accessible newsletters are not just ethical — they perform better across all segments.",
      "The death of open-rate vanity metrics is accelerating. Apple's Mail Privacy Protection, which preloads tracking pixels, has made open rates unreliable since 2021, and competing clients are following suit. Smart publishers have shifted to click-through rate, click-to-open rate, reply rate, and conversion rate as their primary metrics. If you are still reporting open rates to stakeholders as a measure of success, you are measuring noise. Focus on engagement actions that cannot be faked by a privacy proxy.",
